0..74 Comment "// Two composites of substitutions act alike on every term when they agree"
75..149 Comment "// at every index. At an abstraction both composites unfold by conversion,"
150..218 Comment "// lifting being a constructor (`substTwiceUnderLam`; with lifting a"
219..295 Comment "// definition the step is refused, #761, `pathological/desc/lc`). The lifted"
296..358 Comment "// step reads a lookup under one binder as the weakened lookup"
359..431 Comment "// (`lookWeakens`), pushes the weakening through the lifted substitution"
432..479 Comment "// (`substWeaken`), and weakens the hypothesis."
481..553 Comment "// The naturals; the syntax; the congruences; the lemmas the lifted step"
554..562 Comment "// uses."
